            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0259" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G/379: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-09T16:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. Your No. 40, December 9, 11 a.m. No change in list of Latin-American truce
                    membership given on page 81 of Department’s instructions with the exception that
                    the adhesion of Venezuela has expired. Bolivia and Ecuador are still considered
                    members of truce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
